      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Intestinal nonrotation has been recognized as a cause of obstruction in neonates and children. However, it can also be the cause of significant abdominal pain in adults. The pain is recurrent and often associated with a feeling of distention. If the diagnosis is entertained, it often can be made from basic clinical information."},
